    <string name="how_to_play_title">How to play</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_back">Back to menu</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_swipe_hint">Swipe left/right for next/previous rule</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_step1_title">Choosing your move</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_step1_body">Each turn, you project your current speed forward. From this coasted position, you must choose any of the 8 neighboring positions or the coast itself as your next turn.</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_step2_title">Walls and crashing</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_step2_body">Walls block any move whose path crosses them. If your coast projects past a wall and every move would cross it, you crash and are out of the race. Plan your braking early: the faster you go, the longer it takes to slow down.</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_step3_title">Finish line and laps</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_step3_body">Cross the finish line in the direction of its arrow to complete a lap. Whoever completes all laps first wins. Crossing the line against the arrow crashes you instead.</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_step4_title">Oil spills</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_step4_body">Driving over an oil spill takes away your steering for the next turn. The coast is always offered, plus two randomly chosen nearby points — you get a choice, but not the usual one. Slow down before a spill, or steer around it.</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_step5_title">Nails</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_step5_body">Nails force a slowdown. At speed, only the three hardest-braking moves remain. At speed one or less, you can stop, coast forward, or strafe sideways — but you cannot accelerate. Pick your line carefully before hitting nails.</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_step6_title">Gravel trap</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_step6_body">Beyond the outer wall lies a gravel trap. When it is on, running wide is no crash: the gravel brakes you on every move from it and on the two after. The barrier at its far edge stops you like a wall. When it is off, the outer wall stops you as before.</string>

