    <!-- Captions for the gravel_trap walkthrough, from
         tools/tutorial-editor/projects/gravel_trap.json. -->
    <string name="how_to_play_gravel_trap_caption_1">Beyond the outer wall lies a gravel trap, two grid points deep, with a barrier at its far edge.</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_gravel_trap_caption_2">With the gravel trap on, running wide is no crash: points in the gravel are legal moves.</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_gravel_trap_caption_3">In the gravel the car is braked: its coast point is pulled back two grid points.</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_gravel_trap_caption_4">You choose around the braked point as usual. Points past the barrier are withheld, like those past a wall.</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_gravel_trap_caption_5">Every move from the gravel is braked; at low speed you may stop or crawl one point in any direction.</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_gravel_trap_caption_6">Back on the track, the brake holds for two more moves, then you can speed up again.</string>
